{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L17g2jrvv9NycKEqkToqJc","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 3418772d643654b00471e767969242c88a42c314\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 14:42:36 2026 -0600\n\n    own_records marker replaces the three hand-copied deselect lists (#237)\n    \n    Item #229 build-04's fourth attempt failed because select-tests mapped a\n    common.py/build.py change to the whole suite and the gate ran\n    test_no_invocation_lacks_record, which read build-04's own .started\n    marker as a dead invocation. That test was one of the seven doctor tests\n    that read this repository's own records, told apart from the rest of the\n    suite by three hand-copied --deselect lists that stayed in sync only by\n    convention -- and the list was missing it.\n    \n    @pytest.mark.own_records already existed and already had a guard\n    (test_own_records_guard.py) enforcing that every test reading this\n    repository's own records carries it. This closes the gap: the six\n    doctor tests gain the marker, [tests].run and ci.yml's full-suite step\n    become `-m 'not own_records'`, the doctor job and the inherit path run\n    `-m own_records`, every --deselect and DESELECT_FLAGS list is gone, and\n    the guard's exemption for the doctor tests goes with it.\n    \n    Also lands the bucket line: a fix item's spec names the root-cause\n    bucket it closes with `Bucket: <slug>`, and spec-gate refuses a slug\n    attest/buckets.md does not list before any criterion runs. buckets.md\n    lists the five buckets from the 2026-09-27 convergence ruling.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .github/workflows/ci.yml        | 12 +++------","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"335d471e-4a04-47f8-979b-d240ee0c539b","uuid":"a792997b-9d9d-4323-b014-80928a92e331","timestamp":"2026-09-27T21:18:53.438Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 3418772d643654b00471e767969242c88a42c314\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 14:42:36 2026 -0600\n\n    own_records marker replaces the three hand-copied deselect lists (#237)\n    \n    Item #229 build-04's fourth attempt failed because select-tests mapped a\n    common.py/build.py change to the whole suite and the gate ran\n    test_no_invocation_lacks_record, which read build-04's own .started\n    marker as a dead invocation. That test was one of the seven doctor tests\n    that read this repository's own records, told apart from the rest of the\n    suite by three hand-copied --deselect lists that stayed in sync only by\n    convention -- and the list was missing it.\n    \n    @pytest.mark.own_records already existed and already had a guard\n    (test_own_records_guard.py) enforcing that every test reading this\n    repository's own records carries it. This closes the gap: the six\n    doctor tests gain the marker, [tests].run and ci.yml's full-suite step\n    become `-m 'not own_records'`, the doctor job and the inherit path run\n    `-m own_records`, every --deselect and DESELECT_FLAGS list is gone, and\n    the guard's exemption for the doctor tests goes with it.\n    \n    Also lands the bucket line: a fix item's spec names the root-cause\n    bucket it closes with `Bucket: <slug>`, and spec-gate refuses a slug\n    attest/buckets.md does not list before any criterion runs. buckets.md\n    lists the five buckets from the 2026-09-27 convergence ruling.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n .github/workflows/ci.yml        | 12 +++------","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
